OL,3,GNEWSAOysters from nursery 'thriving' in
OL,4,ANorth Sea
OL,5,
OL,6,FOysters which conservationists hope
OL,7,Fwill improve water quality for years to
OL,8,Fcome are "thriving" in the North Sea,
OL,9,Fthey say.
OL,11,FAbout 1,000 mature native oysters and
OL,12,F15,000 juveniles, known as spat on
OL,13,Fshells, have been released at a nursery
OL,14,Fat South Tyneside in the final stages
OL,15,Fof a project.
OL,17,FFor the past six years, the Zoological
OL,18,FSociety of London (ZSL) and nature
OL,19,Fcharity Groundwork have been
OL,20,Festablishing self-sustaining,
OL,21,Ffunctioning oyster reefs in Sunderland
OL,22,Fand off the coast of Whitburn.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,396,390,260,160,0,100
